  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Emergency Response to Conflict Affected Internally Displaced Populations and Communities in Cabo Delgado, Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For over three years, the province of Cabo Delgado province in Mozambique has experienced brutal attacks by armed groups. As a result of insecurity in Cabo Delgado, the humanitarian situation is deteriorating in both hosting and displaced communities, and for those left behind. The situation in Northern Mozambique, facing a triple humanitarian crisis with a conflict, reoccurring impact of natural disasters and the COVID-19 pandemic has become incredibly complex. The objective of the project is to provide live-saving multisectoral response and COVID-19 prevention and mitigation assistance for displaced people and host communities in Northern Mozambique. Building directly on its existing field presence and structures, with added value and comparative advantage on the response, IOM proposes to respond to the immediate humanitarian needs by providing emergency humanitarian assistance using a multisectoral and people-centred approach, increasing local capacity and (human) resources.</narrative>
  </description>
